        "agent_output": "Perfect! All tests pass now. \n\n## Summary\n\nI found and fixed the bug in the markdown table parser. The issue was in `/markdown/extensions/tables.py` at **line 54**.\n\n**The Bug:**\n```python\nis_table = row0_len < 1\n```\n\nThis condition was checking if the number of cells in a row is **less than 1** (i.e., empty), which would only mark completely empty rows as tables. This prevented any actual tables from being recognized.\n\n**The Fix:**\n```python\nis_table = row0_len > 1\n```\n\nNow it correctly identifies rows with **more than 1 cell** as potential tables, which allows the table parser to properly validate the remaining rows and process the table with attribute lists.\n\nThe test that was failing (`test_table_td`) now passes, and all 776 tests in the suite pass successfully.\n",
